("h2","Common questions"),
("qa","Why do private equity firms use so much debt?","Debt means the firm puts in less of its own money, so the same profit is a bigger return on what it invested."),
("qa","What makes a good LBO candidate?","Steady cash flow, low need for big spending, a strong market position and room to improve."),
("qa","What is the risk of an LBO?","If the business struggles, the debt payments can become too much, and the company could go bankrupt."),
